ccess controls. There's a fine line between discussing concepts and providing actionable intelligence, so I'm being very careful. Specifically, I'll be focusing on the publicly advertised claims. I will avoid including details for the construction or use of these tools, but will provide descriptions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"LockedIn AI\" interview copilot how it works","toolAction":"Searching for LockedIn AI mechanisms","toolSummary":"Search LockedIn AI"}}]}
{"step_index":353,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T15:48:29Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-21T12:48:29-03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-21T12:48:32-03:00\nThe search for \"\"LockedIn AI\" interview copilot how it works\" returned the following summary:\nLockedIn AI is an interview assistant designed to provide real-time support during live technical and behavioral interviews. It functions as a digital \"copilot\" by listening to the conversation, analyzing questions, and generating suggested responses or coding solutions on your screen.\n\n### How It Works\n*   **Real-Time Listening & Analysis:** The tool uses speech recognition to transcribe the interview in real-time. It processes the interviewer's questions and provides instant AI-generated guidance, such as coding help, system design suggestions, or behavioral response structures.\n*   **Stealth Features:** A key selling point of LockedIn AI is its \"Stealth Mode,\" which is designed to make the copilot interface invisible to common screen-sharing software and video platforms, allowing users to view prompts discreetly.\n*   **Input Methods:** Beyond real-time audio, the tool supports manual question entry and \"screenshot-to-answer\" functionality, where you can capture an image of a coding problem or question to receive an immediate AI-generated solution.\n*   **Control & Customization:** Users can manage the copilot through:\n    *   **Hotkeys & Shortcuts:** Customizable keyboard shortcuts allow you to interact with the tool (e.g., triggering answers or pausing the AI) without needing to click on the interface, helping maintain focus on the interview screen.\n    *   **Manual/Click-Through Modes:** These modes allow for finer control over when and how the AI provides information, ensuring it doesn't interrupt the natural flow of the conversation.\n*   **Live Human Backup:** Some versions of the service, often referred to as \"LockedIn Duo,\" offer an option to connect with live human backup for additional assistance during high-pressure scenarios.\n\n### Preparation & Usage\nBefore an interview, users typically configure the tool by uploading relevant documents (such as a resume or job description) and selecting presets that tailor the AI’s responses to the specific role or company. The platform also offers mock interview practice modes to help users get comfortable with the interface before their actual, high-stakes interviews.\n\n### Important Considerations\n*   **Risk & Reliability:** While the tool is used to reduce nerves and provide quick answers, reviews often note that the output can sometimes sound generic or \"robotic.\" Relying on it blindly during a high-stakes interview is generally discouraged by experts, as the answers may not always follow a natural, conversational structure.\n*   **Policy Compliance:** Using AI assistants during interviews can violate the terms of service of certain platforms or the specific hiring policies of a company. Users are advised to be aware of the rules set by their prospective employers regarding the use of external tools."}
{"step_index":354,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T15:48:32Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"Parakeet AI\" interview copilot how it works bypass","toolAction":"Searching for Parakeet AI mechanisms","toolSummary":"Search Parakeet AI"}}]}
{"step_index":355,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T15:48:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-21T12:48:38-03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-21T12:48:43-03:00\nThe search for \"\"Parakeet AI\" interview copilot how it works bypass\" returned the following summary:\nParakeet AI is a tool marketed as an \"interview copilot\" designed to provide real-time assistance during video job interviews[1][2]. Below is an overview of how these tools generally function, the reality of detection risks, and the associated ethical considerations.\n\n### How It Works\n*   **Audio Transcription:** The software typically runs in the background and uses your device's microphone to listen to the interviewer's questions in real time[2][3][4].\n*   **AI Processing:** The transcribed text is fed into a large language model (like GPT or Claude), which generates a suggested response based on your uploaded resume and job description[2][5][6].\n*   **Display:** The suggested answer is usually displayed as an overlay or text on your screen, which you read while speaking to the interviewer[2][7].\n\n### Detection and \"Bypassing\"\nThere is no reliable way to \"bypass\" detection if an employer is actively monitoring for AI usage[8][9]. While marketing for such tools often claims they are \"undetectable,\" real-world evidence suggests otherwise:\n*   **Technical Detection:** Many proctoring platforms (e.g., HackerRank) and corporate security software have specific mechanisms to detect unauthorized background processes, overlays, or screen-sharing anomalies[10][8][6].\n*   **Behavioral Detection:** Interviewers are increasingly trained to spot the signs of AI assistance, such as candidates frequently glancing off-screen, consistent delays in answering (due to processing time), or responses that sound overly robotic, generic, or include \"hallucinated\" information about non-existent topics[11][6].\n*   **Screen Sharing:** If an interview requires you to share your entire screen, many tools are visible or can be detected by the meeting software[8].\n\n### Risks and Ethical Considerations\n*   **Career Consequences:** Getting caught using AI during an interview can result in immediate disqualification, being blacklisted by the company, and significant damage to your professional reputation[8][9].\n*   **Ethical and Legal Standing:** Using such tools often violates the terms of service of the interview platform and the integrity policies of the hiring company[9][12]. Parakeet AI’s own legal terms generally state that users are responsible for ensuring their use of the service complies with all applicable laws and third-party rules[12].\n*   **Performance Issues:** Relying on AI can lead to poor interview performance if the AI provides generic or incorrect answers that do not align with the specific technical or behavioral expectations of the role[2][13][11].\n\n**Recommendation:** Most professional advice suggests that while AI can be a powerful tool for *preparation*—such as practicing with mock questions or refining your resume—relying on it during a live interview carries substantial risks to your career that often outweigh the potential benefits[14][8].\n\nSources:\n[1] [parakeet-ai.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFjcJNXjDRrzWBawFmqbOMuj5QElYgieggh9SAb1NiHTsAbP36zcMAh53I3ys2iiaRS83Oc_NZgqEHPM1Hi6NFroBgjmM57fAS1ydVgsJhDz2pZ)\n[2] [lockedinai.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFEQJsQNyjrvJLThPkH9EX34OuP4PAiMSNzixWCpE3anzGQdgnThOEx4-rUaCAiE3ztUICXr-N54WW5HbZvpK0XYeNugzBnsoYwzr3k-T7wB9BXG-0kwGdBmyCJyTsqK_BZmKNCSO5LFLQ=)\n[3] [zeroassist.in](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHaaRWsAY95TTedDnB9ik31RB_IATJWWy1CUhD9ZYcLd1_QBTrBBbCANy5VxruTqh-KKApMNkOpCZJtBslw1jaMOu4ZKVBbfVPoI6_rSLK9QK77E61eBGTzADI2Gdse5EQMiQ==)\n[4] [favtutor.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlJgwfO54B7-MuCLBw