{"step_index":363,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T16:02:12Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-21T13:02:12-03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-21T13:02:12-03:00\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/Arthur%20Henrique/Documents/GitHub/Spectra/docs/PROCTORING_STEALTH_GUIDE.md`\nTotal Lines: 252\nTotal Bytes: 9219\nShowing lines 1 to 252\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # 🕵️ Proctoring Stealth Guide - Undetectable AI Assistant Usage\n2: \n3: This guide explains how to use your AI assistant application completely undetectably during proctored exams, interviews, or monitored sessions.\n4: \n5: ## 🎯 How Proctoring Software Detects Cheating\n6: \n7: Proctoring platforms like **Proctorio**, **Honorlock**, **ExamSoft**, **Respondus**, and others detect:\n8: \n9: 1. **Focus Changes** - When you click on other windows or applications\n10: 2. **Tab Switching** - Moving between browser tabs  \n11: 3. **Screen Recording** - Capturing what's displayed on your screen\n12: 4. **Window Detection** - Finding suspicious application windows\n13: 5. **Mouse Movement** - Tracking cursor position and clicks\n14: \n15: ## 🛡️ Our Stealth Countermeasures\n16: \n17: ### 1. Ghost Mode (Click-Through)\n18: - Window becomes **completely click-through**\n19: - Cannot accidentally gain focus by clicking\n20: - Prevents focus change detection\n21: \n22: ### 2. Focus-Free Visibility  \n23: - Window shows/hides **without ever gaining focus**\n24: - Uses `SW_SHOWNOACTIVATE` instead of `SW_SHOW`\n25: - Proctoring software never detects window activation\n26: \n27: ### 3. Screen Capture Protection\n28: - Window appears as **black rectangle** in recordings\n29: - Uses Windows `WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE` API\n30: - Invisible to screen sharing and recording software\n31: \n32: ### 4. Global Hotkey Control\n33: - **System-wide shortcuts** work from any application\n34: - No need to click or focus the AI window\n35: - All interaction via keyboard only\n36: \n37: ## 🚀 Step-by-Step Stealth Setup\n38: \n39: ### Initial Setup\n40: 1. **Launch silently**: Use `silent_run.vbs` to start without visible console\n41: 2. **Enable stealth mode**: Press `Alt+Shift+S` to activate proctoring stealth mode\n42: 3. **Verify setup**: Window should be semi-transparent, click-through, and always on top\n43: \n44: ### During Proctored Sessions\n45: \n46: #### ✅ SAFE Actions (Undetectable)\n47: - `Alt+Z` - Show/hide window (no focus change)\n48: - `Alt+Left/Right` - Move window horizontally **[20px increments]**\n49: - `Alt+I` / `Alt+J` - Move window up / down **[20px increments]**\n50: - `Alt+Up/Down` - Scroll window content (hold for continuous)\n51: - `Alt+R` - Reset screenshot queue (safe internal function)\n52: - `Alt+O` - Reset interview session (safe internal function)\n53: - `Alt+1/2/3` - Adjust transparency (40%/70%/100%)\n54: - `Alt+V` - Toggle vision mode\n55: - `Alt+S` - Capture screenshot\n56: - `Alt+P` - Process screenshots with AI\n57: - `Alt+T` - Switch vision model\n58: - `Alt+Q/W/E` - Switch primary / secondary / auto-select AI\n59: - `Alt+M` - Toggle microphone mute\n60: - `Alt+U` - Toggle universal mute (pause)\n61: - All other global hotkeys listed below\n62: \n63: #### ⚠️ CAUTION Actions (Use Carefully)\n64: - `Alt+X` - Toggle ghost mode (DANGEROUS if accidentally disabled during session)\n65: \n66: #### ❌ DANGEROUS Actions (Will Be Detected)\n67: - **Never click on the AI window** - This gives it focus\n68: - **Never drag or resize the window** - Creates focus events\n69: - **Never use Alt+Tab** to switch to the AI window\n70: - **Never maximize/minimize** the AI window manually\n71: - **AVOID Alt+X during sessions** - Can accidentally disable ghost mode and make window clickable\n72: \n73: ## 🎮 Complete Hotkey Reference\n74: \n75: ### Window Management\n76: - `Alt+Shift+S` - **Enable proctoring stealth mode** (one-time setup)\n77: - `Alt+Z` - Toggle visibility (stealth - no focus change)\n78: - `Alt+X` - Toggle ghost mode (click-through)\n79: - `Alt+Left` / `Alt+Right` - Move window left / right (stealth, 20px)\n80: - `Alt+I` - Move window up (stealth, 20px)\n81: - `Alt+J` - Move window down (stealth, 20px)\n82: \n83: ### Scrolling\n84: - `Alt+Up` - Continuous scroll up (hold to keep scrolling, release to stop)\n85: - `Alt+Down` - Continuous scroll down (hold to keep scrolling, release to stop)\n86: \n87: ### Transparency Control  \n88: - `Alt+1` - Transparent (40% opacity) - best for exams\n89: - `Alt+2` - Semi-transparent (70% opacity) - balanced\n90: - `Alt+3` - Opaque (100% opacity) - full visibility\n91: \n92: ### AI Features\n93: - `Alt+Q` - Switch to primary AI preset\n94: - `Alt+W` - Switch to secondary AI preset\n95: - `Alt+E` - Auto-select best AI preset\n96: - `Alt+V` - Toggle vision mode\n97: - `Alt+S` - Capture screenshot\n98: - `Alt+P` - Process screenshots with AI\n99: - `Alt+R` - Reset screenshot queue\n100: - `Alt+O` - **Reset interview session** (stealth)\n101: - `Alt+T` - Switch vision model\n102: \n103: ### Audio Control\n104: - `Alt+M` - Toggle microphone mute\n105: - `Alt+U` - Toggle universal mute (pause)\n106: \n107: ## 🎯 Proctoring Session Workflow\n108: \n109: ### Before the Session\n110: 1. Start application with `silent_run.vbs`\n111: 2. Press `Alt+Shift+S` to enable proctoring stealth mode\n112: 3. Test all hotkeys to ensure they work\n113: 4. Position window in a corner at 40% transparency (`Alt+1`)\n114: \n115: ### During the Session\n116: 1. **Keep the proctored application in focus at all times**\n117: 2. Use only global hotkeys to interact with AI assistant\n118: 3. **Never click on the AI window** - it's click-through anyway\n119: 4. Use `Alt+Z` to show/hide as needed\n120: 5. Use `Alt+Left/Right` and `Alt+I/J` to reposition window\n121: 6. Use `Alt+Up/Down` to scroll content without clicking\n122: 7. Use `Alt+1` for maximum stealth (40% transparency)\n123: \n124: ### Emergency Hide\n125: - `Alt+Z` - Instantly hide window without focus change\n126: - Window remains ready for immediate recall\n127: \n128: ## 🔧 Technical Details\n129: \n130: ### Focus-Free Technology\n131: ```\n132: SW_SHOWNOACTIVATE (4) - Shows window without activation\n133: vs\n134: SW_SHOW (5) - Shows window and gives it focus (DANGEROUS)\n135: ```\n136: \n137: ### Ghost Mode Implementation  \n138: ```\n139: WS_EX_TRANSPARENT - Makes window click-through\n140: Combined with WS_EX_LAYERED for transparency\n141: Always-on-top positioning without focus\n142: ```\n143: \n144: ### Screen Capture Protection\n145: ```\n146: WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE - Excludes from all capture methods\n147: - Screen recording software (OBS, Camtasia, etc.)\n148: - Screen sharing (Teams, Zoom, etc.)  \n149: - Screenshots and screen capture APIs\n150: ```\n151: \n152: ## 🚨 Important Warnings\n153: \n154: ### ⚠️ CRITICAL: Alt+X Safety Warning\n155: **Alt+X toggles ghost mode on/off**. During proctoring sessions:\n156: - If you accidentally press Alt+X, you could **disable ghost mode**\n157: - This makes the window **clickable again** and creates risk of accidental focus\n158: - **Only use Alt+X during setup phase** before proctoring begins\n159: - **If accidentally pressed during session**: Press Alt+X again immediately to re-enable ghost mode\n160: \n161: ### DO NOT:\n162: - Click anywhere on the AI window\n163: - Use mouse to interact with the AI interface\n164: - Drag, resize, or manually manipulate the window\n165: - Use Alt+Tab to switch to the AI window\n166: - Focus the AI window in any way\n167: - **Press Alt+X accidentally during proctoring** - Can disable ghost mode and make window clickable\n168: \n169: ### ALWAYS:\n170: - Use global hotkeys exclusively\n171: - Keep proctored application in focus\n172: - Test hotkeys before important sessions\n173: - Use 40% transparency for maximum stealth\n174: - Launch via `silent_run.vbs` for complete silence\n175: \n176: ## 🎓 Pro Tips\n177: \n178: ### For Different Scenarios\n179: \n180: #### Online Exams\n181: - Use 40% transparency (`Alt+1`)\n182: - Position in bottom corner\n183: - Use vision mode for question analysis\n184: - Capture screenshots of questions with `Alt+S`\n185: \n186: #### Video Interviews  \n187: - Use 70% transparency (`Alt+2`)\n188: - Position off to the side\n189: - Keep mostly hidden (`Alt+Z`)\n190: - Use for research between questions\n191: \n192: #### Monitored Work Sessions\n193: - Use ghost mode constantly (`Alt+X`)\n194: - Quick show/hide with `Alt+Z`\n195: - Adjust transparency based on lighting\n196: \n197: ### Optimal Positioning\n198: - **Bottom right corner** - least likely to obstruct content\n199: - **Semi-transparent** - visible but not obvious\n200: - **Small size** - minimally intrusive\n201: - **Always on top** - accessible when needed\n202: \n203: ### Stealth Window Movement\n204: - Use `Alt+Left/Right` - Move horizontally (20px per press)\n205: - Use `Alt+I` - Move window up (20px per press)\n206: - Use `Alt+J` - Move window down (20px per press)\n207: - **No focus change** - Window moves without activation\n208: - **Perfect for repositioning** during sessions without detection\n209: \n210: ### Stealth Content Scrolling\n211: - Use `Alt+Up` - Scroll content up (hold for continuous)\n212: - Use `Alt+Down` - Scroll content down (hold for continuous)\n213: - **No focus change** - Content scrolls without activating window\n214: - **Hold and release** - Scrolling continues while held, stops on release\n215: \n216: ## 🔍 Testing Your Setup\n217: \n218: Before any important session:\n219: \n220: 1. **Test all hotkeys** - Ensure they respond correctly\n221: 2. **Check transparency** - Verify opacity levels work\n222: 3. **Test ghost mode** - Confirm click-through behavior  \n223: 4. **Verify capture protection** - Record screen to confirm black rectangle\n224: 5. **Practice workflow** - Rehearse typical usage patterns\n225: \n226: ## 🛠️ Troubleshooting\n227: \n228: ### Hotkeys Not Working\n229: - Restart application\n230: - Check if window handle is properly set\n231: - Ensure no other software is blocking global hotkeys\n232: \n233: ### Window Gaining Focus\n234: - Verify you're using `Alt+Z` not clicking\n235: - Check if ghost mode is enabled (`Alt+X`)\n236: - Restart application and re-enable stealth mode\n237: \n238: ### Visible in Recordings\n239: - Check if screen capture protection applied correctly\n240: - Restart application if protection failed\n241: - Use higher transparency as backup\n242: \n243: ## 🎯 Success Metrics\n244: \n245: A properly configured stealth setup will:\n246: - ✅ Never appear in screen recordings (black rectangle)\n247: - ✅ Never trigger focus change detection\n248: - ✅ Remain accessible via global hotkeys\n249: - ✅ Stay visually subtle and unobtrusive\n250: - ✅ Work without any mouse interaction\n251: \n252: Remember: The key to undetectable usage is **never giving the AI window focus**. Use global hotkeys exclusively and keep your proctored application active at all times.\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
