{"step_index":367,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T16:02:23Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-21T13:02:23-03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-21T13:02:27-03:00\nThe search for \"\"Parakeet AI\" features \"interview\" \"copilot\" \"pricing\" \"stealth\" \"features\"\" returned the following summary:\nParakeet AI is a real-time interview assistance tool—often referred to as an \"interview copilot\"—designed to help job candidates during live video interviews[1][2][3].\n\n### Core Features\n*   **Real-Time Assistance:** The software listens to interview questions in real-time, transcribes them, and generates suggested responses for the user to read[1][4][3].\n*   **Resume/Context Integration:** Users can upload their CV or job description, which the AI uses to ground its answers in the candidate's actual background and the specific role[1][4].\n*   **Platform Compatibility:** It is designed to work with major video conferencing platforms like Zoom, Google Meet, Microsoft Teams, and Webex, as well as various technical assessment platforms[5][2][3].\n*   **Language Support:** It supports a wide range of languages (reportedly 59)[1][6].\n\n### Pricing\nParakeet AI typically operates on a **credit-based, pay-as-you-go model** rather than a traditional monthly subscription[7][8][4].\n*   **Structure:** Users purchase \"credits,\" where one credit typically covers one hour of live assistance[7].\n*   **Trial:** It often offers a limited free trial (e.g., a set number of short sessions, such as 10 sessions of up to 10 minutes each)[9][10].\n*   **Pricing Variations:** Because it uses an interactive credit system, exact prices can fluctuate or be presented through promotional codes; users are encouraged to check the official site for current credit packages[9][4].\n\n### \"Stealth\" and Detection\n*   **Stealth Claims:** The tool markets itself as a private, \"invisible\" overlay that is not easily seen by standard screen-capture algorithms used in video calls[7][11][4].\n*   **Detection Risks:** Despite these claims, the tool is not foolproof[7]. Its process name may be visible in system monitors (like macOS Activity Monitor or Windows Task Manager)[1][6]. Furthermore, some enterprise proctoring services (e.g., Talview) have specifically identified and included the tool in their detection documentation[7][12][13].\n*   **User Warning:** Using AI interview assistants can violate the terms of service of many employers and platforms[14][5]. Being caught using such tools may result in negative consequences for the candidate[14].\n\n***Disclaimer:** This information is for educational and research purposes. The use of AI tools during interviews may be considered unethical or a violation of company policy; proceed at your own risk[14][5].*\n\nSources:\n[1] [lockedinai.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHAWGmIGYYLFNyWKcrsH7puzbKgEkAgevENS2khcdwekeREsREHPTCD-3Ls0rjtA9XSc3Qyv00zorCLz-BfKYVmieyzxrrYZgIHt4xsgcldA3qn6WrlUnMGxc0C8sfHElovmQgPUsmxpeY=)\n[2] [trustpilot.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHrtZIPwyFYxTofmVpyqpv1hoDdL1KK_lLi797cyz00Jm7ozA9UAqOe81_qvehYDN5tjuKpWdk5iZigCEkF1itT-huXB6Hqv9DkTZigh0FmH9rrcHKdwS0GhZPCs9ZbaN1i-TkKKfq2)\n[3] [autoapplier.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHIwh1AWRIEkX6w-m74bMbu5nc1yxzed5Lws48amdSF6VWPbZO6ArT4q3EUf3KvtIlp_d-JVvel-YvIuBazMQLkP5v0Qaqgn-wWQh2g9UU19ZTt702yszkL7rJ0tGJl_VEWrcMwn84Si7yx1D3Y2ppwuNnGTsMyMiaAf5XZ5Z3m0kXOeGZfq7c_NFbguO3q_pkUgA_ll5tqFo2dZltDlWCM7DQIHyQYLBl9CYAZin5mfCDSvUo=)\n[4] [lockedinai.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHAWGmIGYYLFNyWKcrsH7puzbKgEkAgevENS2khcdwekeREsREHPTCD-3Ls0rjtA9XSc3Qyv00zorCLz-BfKYVmieyzxrrYZgIHt4xsgcldA3qn6WrlUnMGxc0C8sfHElovmQgPUsmxpeY=)\n[5] [skywork.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH-m2EIdScz00ZMcMVvWAP5m3kystLAd4PXOC-hNn0QavdNSA29Fil_jX